# C# + .NET Development Guide

## Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Runtime | .NET 10 |
| Framework | ASP.NET Core |
| Validation | FluentValidation |
| Data | Entity Framework Core |
| Messaging | Rebus |
| Resilience | Polly |
| Testing | xUnit, FluentAssertions, Moq, Testcontainers |
| Logging | Serilog |

## Rule Routing

Consult these rules based on what you are working on:

## Quick Reference

- Build/modify API endpoint: `languages/csharp/controllers.mdc`, `languages/csharp/validation.mdc`, `languages/csharp/error-handling.mdc`
- Build command/query flow: `languages/csharp/mediator.mdc`, `languages/csharp/testing.mdc`
- Data and transactions: `languages/csharp/ef-core.mdc`, `languages/csharp/resilience.mdc`
- Secure/auth changes: `languages/csharp/security.mdc`, `languages/csharp/auth.mdc`, `languages/csharp/input-sanitization.mdc`

### API & Controllers
- Controller conventions, routing, ActionResult → `languages/csharp/controllers.mdc`
- Request validation (FluentValidation) → `languages/csharp/validation.mdc`
- Input sanitization (SQL injection, XSS, path traversal) → `languages/csharp/input-sanitization.mdc`

### Data & Persistence
- EF Core DbContext, repositories, migrations → `languages/csharp/ef-core.mdc`

### CQRS & Messaging
- Mediator pattern (commands, queries, pipeline behaviors) → `languages/csharp/mediator.mdc`
- Rebus messaging (handlers, sagas, outbox) → `languages/csharp/messaging.mdc`

### Cross-Cutting
- Code quality, C# 14 idioms, records, nullable references → `languages/csharp/code-quality.mdc`
- Error handling (ProblemDetails, Result pattern) → `languages/csharp/error-handling.mdc`
- Logging (Serilog, enrichers, correlation IDs) → `languages/csharp/logging.mdc`
- Security (secrets, HTTPS, headers, CORS) → `languages/csharp/security.mdc`
- Auth (JWT Bearer, policy-based, claims) → `languages/csharp/auth.mdc`
- Resilience (Polly retry, circuit breaker, timeout) → `languages/csharp/resilience.mdc`
- Testing (xUnit, FluentAssertions, Moq) → `languages/csharp/testing.mdc`
- Dependencies (NuGet, Central Package Management) → `languages/csharp/dependencies.mdc`

### Architecture Patterns (request when needed)
- Clean Architecture, CQRS, DDD → `patterns/architecture.mdc`
- Clean code principles → `patterns/clean-code.mdc`
- CQRS details → `patterns/cqrs.mdc`
- API design conventions → `patterns/api-design.mdc`

## Key Conventions

- **Error handling:** Result pattern for domain errors; global exception middleware; RFC 7807 ProblemDetails
- **Validation:** FluentValidation at API boundaries
- **Testing:** TDD; xUnit; FluentAssertions; Moq for mocks
- **Logging:** Serilog with structured properties and correlation IDs
- **Dependencies:** Central Package Management; only compatible licenses
